From: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] udev: use SDSP and the kernel mount matrix on Nabu

Nabu exposes its physical SSC sensors through SDSP. Advertising ADSP as a
second source can register duplicate accelerometers and make desktop
orientation depend on probe order.

Select SDSP as the sole SSC owner and publish its kernel/Device Tree
mount_matrix through ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX, the standard udev property consumed
by iio-sensor-proxy. This keeps the board transform in firmware description
instead of duplicating it in a GNOME- or user-specific workaround.

---
 data/80-iio-sensor-proxy.rules | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/80-iio-sensor-proxy.rules b/data/80-iio-sensor-proxy.rules
index 9245181..b45f124 100644
--- a/data/80-iio-sensor-proxy.rules
+++ b/data/80-iio-sensor-proxy.rules
@@ -21,5 +21,9 @@ SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_ACCELEROMETER}=="1", ENV{IIO_SENSOR_PROXY_TYPE}
-# Set the sensor type for all the types we recognise for SDSP/ADSP with libssc.
-# Some devices expose the sensors via a separate SDSP while others re-use ADSP.
-# These DSPs expose itself as /dev/fastrpc-* in the misc subsystem.
-SUBSYSTEM=="misc", KERNEL=="fastrpc-adsp*", ENV{IIO_SENSOR_PROXY_TYPE}+="ssc-accel ssc-light ssc-compass"
-SUBSYSTEM=="misc", KERNEL=="fastrpc-sdsp*", ENV{IIO_SENSOR_PROXY_TYPE}+="ssc-accel ssc-light ssc-compass"
+# Nabu exposes its physical SSC sensors through SDSP. Do not advertise ADSP as
+# a second source, otherwise two accelerometers can race for SensorProxy.
+SUBSYSTEM=="misc", KERNEL=="fastrpc-adsp*", ENV{IIO_SENSOR_PROXY_TYPE}=""
+SUBSYSTEM=="misc", KERNEL=="fastrpc-sdsp*", ENV{IIO_SENSOR_PROXY_TYPE}="ssc-accel ssc-light ssc-compass"
+
+# Publish the kernel/Device Tree orientation through the standard udev property
+# consumed by iio-sensor-proxy. The parser remains responsible for validating
+# the matrix and falls back safely if the sysfs value is malformed.
+SUBSYSTEM=="misc", KERNEL=="fastrpc-sdsp*", TEST=="mount_matrix", ENV{ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX}="$attr{mount_matrix}"
-- 
2.52.0
